  "name": "Beginner 3-9: Final Project \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Panelized Tower with Surface Normal Extrusions",
  "brief": "Culmination: Ellipse\u00e2\u2020\u2019LinearArray\u00e2\u2020\u2019Rotate/Scale(GenePool)\u00e2\u2020\u2019Loft\u00e2\u2020\u2019Diamond Panels + Area\u00e2\u2020\u2019SurfaceClosestPoint\u00e2\u2020\u2019EvaluateSurface\u00e2\u2020\u2019Normal\u00e2\u2020\u2019Move\u00e2\u2020\u2019ExtrudePoint\u00e2\u2020\u2019CustomPreview",
  "version": "1.0",
  "created": "2026-02-23T04:07:16.958741Z",
  "context": "Final project combining all beginner course concepts. Left-to-right pipeline: Left section (purple): Ellipse stack pipeline \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Point \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Ellipse \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Linear Array \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Gene Pool Rotate/Scale \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Loft \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Diamond Panels (sliders for U/V divisions and scale). \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Custom Preview. Creates the panelized tower form. Right section (white): Normal extrusion pipeline \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Area: extracts centroids of diamond panels. Surface Closest Point: finds UV coordinates on the lofted surface for each panel centroid. Evaluate Surface: gets surface Normal at each UV point. Amplitude \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Vector Display: visualizes normals. Multiplication: scales normals by a factor (slider=0.15). Move: offsets panel centroids along scaled normals. Extrude Point: extrudes diamond panels toward the offset points. \u00e2\u2020\u2019 Custom Preview ('white' color). Result: a diamond-panelized tower with panels extruded along surface normals \u00e2\u20ac\u201d a complete architectural facade.",
